{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1223853-2e-lodge-of-silver","id":1223853,"title":"[2E] Lodge of Silver","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-01T01:32:26-07:00","id":1223853,"title":"[2E] Lodge of Silver","content":"Having blessing and being inspired by this post of <b>Nofather</b>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1223717#post1223717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd be surprised if there wasn't a lodge of werewolves dedicated to the destruction of silver in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>So here is opening concept that I will edit and expand with coming ideas.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lodge of Silver</b></span><br /> ???,???,???<br /> <br /> Silver. Ultimate Bane of every Uratha. From the time of Sundering \u2013 some even say that in Pangea \u2013 silver was sure doom of werewolves. Not surprising that were created Lodge dedicated to fight with this threat to Uratha race.<br /> ???<br /> In times Vikings ( see <i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> in <b>Dark Eras </b>1 ) ??? were valuable assets of the packs as silver was main currency of Early Medieval Europe. Adherents were used as \u2018silver fever\u2019 hunters, sensing possible loot and where Norseman should go to.<br /> <br /> <b>TOTEM:</b> ???<br /> ( Was thinking about Silver Wolf <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209584-are-there-secondborn\">Secondborn</a> here, but would want to use also Forsaken adherents of the Lodge. :/ )<br /> <br /> <b>BONDS</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Adherents of Silver are more resistant to Moon Metal than normal Uratha. They take only half of damage made from silver. Pure adherents also reacts just like Forsaken werewolves to the touch of silver.<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To find weaponized silver.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban</b>: ??? ( Cannot touch not blessed by Totem silver? But then it would be weird one for \u2018silver seeking\u2019 Uratha at Vikings times )<br /> <br /> <b>SACRED HUNT</b><br /> The Lodge\u2019s Sacred Hunt let adherents to sense silver in his vicinity. He sees reflects of silver past any concealment or objects in the range of 50 times his Primal Urge in meters. ( Maybe 500 * Primal Urge meters instead? )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TOOLS</b><br /> ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T02:25:52-07:00","id":1223860,"title":"","content":"So who are their sacred prey? I don\u2019t remember any other 2E lodges hunting literal objects as theirs, or were there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T02:36:48-07:00","id":1223862,"title":"","content":"Quoting Master Chris Allen...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868511#post868511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lodges possess refinements of the sacred hunt. In some cases this is a specific type of prey; in other cases, it is something else to do with the hunt, such as an element of the context or the pursuit or the kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in that broad sense Sacred Hunting of Silver is okay. Even if not, we can use Spirits of Silver - but it would not be as much powerful and generally 'real silver' like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Po